---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import data from "../../data/velocity.json";
import { NICKNAMES, slug, summarize } from "../../lib/velocity.js";

const s = summarize(data);
const { first, last } = s;
const pct = (x: number, d = 0) => `${(x * 100).toFixed(d)}%`;
const r2 = (x: number) => x.toFixed(2);
const recent = data.seasons.find((x) => x.season === 2020)!.league;
const sinceFlat = last.ff - recent.ff;
const champRanks = s.champs.map((c) => c.rank);
const worstChamp = Math.max(...champRanks);
const bestChamp = Math.min(...champRanks);
const q = s.pitchers.sp.quartiles;
const top = s.yoy.bands;
const latestTeams = data.seasons[data.seasons.length - 1].teams;
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const ordinal = (n: number) => {
  const sx = ["th", "st", "nd", "rd"], v = n % 100;
  return n + (sx[(v - 20) % 10] || sx[v] || sx[0]);
};
---
<Base
  title="Pitchers Keep Throwing Harder"
  description={`MLB four-seam velocity, ${first.season}–${last.season}, and what it is worth to pitchers and teams.`}
>
  <article>
    <header class="measure">
      <p class="kicker">Velocity</p>
      <h1>Pitchers Keep Throwing Harder. Here’s What the Speed Buys.</h1>
      <p class="dek">
        The average four-seam fastball has gained {s.gain.toFixed(1)} mph since {first.season}, most of it in the last
        five seasons. Velocity reliably buys strikeouts. It buys wins less reliably.
      </p>
      <p class="byline">Regular-season pitches, {first.season}–{last.season} · Updated {data.meta.generated}</p>
    </header>

    <div class="measure">
      <p>
        In {first.season}, the average major league four-seam fastball crossed the plate at {first.ff.toFixed(1)} mph. For
        five seasons, it barely moved. Then it started climbing, and it has not stopped: {last.ff.toFixed(1)} mph in
        {last.season}, a gain of {sinceFlat.toFixed(1)} mph since 2020 alone.
      </p>
      <p>
        The average hides how much the whole distribution has shifted. In {first.season}, {pct(first.share95)} of
        four-seamers reached 95 mph. In {last.season}, {pct(last.share95)} did.
      </p>
    </div>

    <figure class="wide" id="lead">
      <div class="chart-head">
        <h3>How fast four-seam fastballs are thrown, by season</h3>
        <p>Share of all regular-season four-seamers at each speed. The vertical tick marks the season’s average.</p>
      </div>
      <ul class="legend">
        <li><span class="swatch" style="background: var(--r4); opacity: 0.55"></span>Under 95 mph</li>
        <li><span class="swatch" style="background: var(--r2)"></span>95 mph or faster</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="chart" data-chart="ridge"></div>
      <figcaption>Source: Baseball Savant (Statcast). {last.season} includes {last.ffN.toLocaleString()} four-seamers.</figcaption>
    </figure>

    <div class="measure">
      <h2>It isn’t only the bullpen</h2>
      <p>
        Relievers throw harder than starters, and teams have handed relievers a bigger share of innings, from
        {pct(first.reliefShareIP)} in {first.season} to {pct(last.reliefShareIP)} in {last.season}. That accounts for some of
        the rise, but not most of it. Starters gained {(last.ffSP - first.ffSP).toFixed(1)} mph over the decade, more than
        relievers did ({(last.ffRP - first.ffRP).toFixed(1)} mph).
      </p>
    </div>

    <figure class="measure">
      <div class="chart-head">
        <h3>Average four-seam velocity, starters vs. relievers</h3>
        <p>Weighted by four-seamers thrown. A pitcher counts as a starter if at least half his appearances were starts.</p>
      </div>
      <ul class="legend">
        <li><span class="swatch line" style="background: var(--s2)"></span>Relievers</li>
        <li><span class="swatch line" style="background: var(--s1)"></span>Starters</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="chart" data-chart="roles"></div>
    </figure>

    <div class="measure">
      <p>
        The hardest throwers have pulled away the most. Four-seamers at 98 mph or more, once a novelty, made up
        {pct(first.share98, 1)} of the total in {first.season} and {pct(last.share98, 1)} in {last.season}.
      </p>
    </div>

    <figure class="measure">
      <div class="chart-head">
        <h3>Share of four-seamers thrown 98 mph or faster</h3>
      </div>
      <div class="chart" data-chart="share98"></div>
    </figure>

    <div class="measure">
      <h2>Speed buys strikeouts</h2>
      <p>
        For an individual pitcher, velocity’s clearest payoff is the strikeout. Among starters, the correlation between
        fastball speed and strikeout rate is {r2(s.pitchers.sp.k)}; among relievers, {r2(s.pitchers.rp.k)}. The link to
        preventing runs is real but weaker: {r2(s.pitchers.sp.era)} with ERA for starters, {r2(s.pitchers.rp.era)} for
        relievers. A strikeout is only one way to get an out, and plenty of soft-tossers succeed by limiting hard contact.
      </p>
      <p>
        Wins are weaker still ({r2(s.pitchers.sp.w)} for starters), because a pitcher’s win total depends heavily on his
        team’s hitting and bullpen. Still, the gap adds up over a season. The hardest-throwing quarter of starters
        averaged a {q.fast.era.toFixed(2)} ERA and {q.fast.w.toFixed(1)} wins; the softest-throwing quarter, a
        {q.slow.era.toFixed(2)} ERA and {q.slow.w.toFixed(1)} wins.
      </p>
    </div>

    <figure class="measure">
      <div class="chart-head">
        <h3>Fastball velocity vs. results, one season at a time</h3>
        <p>Each dot is a pitcher who threw at least {data.meta.minFF} four-seamers and {data.meta.minIP.SP} innings as a starter or {data.meta.minIP.RP} in relief (scaled down for 2020’s 60-game season).</p>
      </div>
      <div class="seg" role="group" aria-label="Measure" data-metric>
        <button type="button" data-metric="k" aria-pressed="true">Strikeout %</button>
        <button type="button" data-metric="era" aria-pressed="false">ERA</button>
        <button type="button" data-metric="w" aria-pressed="false">Wins (starters)</button>
      </div>
      <div class="seg" role="group" aria-label="Season" data-pseason>
        {data.seasons.map((x) => (
          <button type="button" data-season={x.season} aria-pressed={x.season === last.season ? "true" : "false"}>{x.season}</button>
        ))}
      </div>
      <ul class="legend" data-role-legend>
        <li><span class="swatch" style="background: var(--s1)"></span>Starters</li>
        <li><span class="swatch" style="background: var(--s2)"></span>Relievers</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="chart" data-chart="pitchers"></div>
      <figcaption>The trend line and correlation cover every pitcher shown.</figcaption>
    </figure>

    <div class="measure">
      <h2>When a pitcher gains speed, he gets better</h2>
      <p>
        Hard throwers may simply be better pitchers to begin with. A cleaner test is to follow the same pitcher from one
        season to the next. Among {s.yoy.n.toLocaleString()} pairs of consecutive seasons, pitchers who added 1.5 mph or
        more raised their strikeout rate by {top.k[4].v.toFixed(1)} percentage points on average and cut their ERA by
        {Math.abs(top.era[4].v).toFixed(2)} runs. Those who lost 1.5 mph or more saw their strikeout rate fall
        {Math.abs(top.k[0].v).toFixed(1)} points and their ERA rise {top.era[0].v.toFixed(2)}.
      </p>
      <p>
        Even pitchers whose speed held steady got a little worse ({top.era[2].v > 0 ? "+" : ""}{top.era[2].v.toFixed(2)} ERA),
        largely because a season good enough to qualify tends to be followed by a more ordinary one. Measured against
        that baseline, the effect of velocity is plain.
      </p>
    </div>

    <figure class="measure">
      <div class="chart-head">
        <h3>Average change from one season to the next, by change in fastball velocity</h3>
        <p>Same pitcher, same role, consecutive seasons. Blue marks an improvement, orange a decline.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="chart" data-chart="yoyK"></div>
      <div class="chart" data-chart="yoyERA" style="margin-top: 20px"></div>
    </figure>

    <div class="measure">
      <h2>Harder-throwing teams win a little more</h2>
      <p>
        Add up a whole staff and the pattern holds, more faintly. Compared with the league average each season, a team’s
        four-seam velocity has a correlation of {r2(s.teams.r)} with its winning percentage. Staffs in the hardest-throwing
        quarter, at least {s.teams.q3.toFixed(1)} mph above average, made the playoffs {pct(s.teams.fastRate)} of the time.
        Staffs in the slowest quarter made it {pct(s.teams.slowRate)} of the time.
      </p>
    </div>

    <figure class="measure">
      <div class="chart-head">
        <h3>Staff velocity vs. regular-season record</h3>
        <p>Each dot is one team-season, {first.season}–{last.season}. Velocity is measured against that season’s league average.</p>
      </div>
      <ul class="legend">
        <li><span class="swatch" style="background: var(--s1)"></span>Made playoffs</li>
        <li><span class="swatch" style="background: var(--udfa); opacity: 0.6"></span>Missed playoffs</li>
        <li><span class="swatch" style="background: var(--s1); box-shadow: 0 0 0 2px var(--ink)"></span>Won World Series</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="chart" data-chart="teams"></div>
    </figure>

    <div class="measure">
      <p>
        The champions tell the same story. Every World Series winner since {first.season} ranked between
        {ordinal(bestChamp)} and {ordinal(worstChamp)} of 30 in staff velocity. {worstChamp <= 15 ? "All of them were in the top half; " : ""}
        {bestChamp > 3 ? "none of them was among the three hardest-throwing staffs." : ""} Velocity helps a team get to
        October. It doesn’t decide what happens there.
      </p>
    </div>

    <figure class="wide">
      <div class="chart-head">
        <h3>Every staff’s velocity, by season</h3>
        <p>Four-seam velocity relative to the league average. Hover a dot for the team; click to open its page.</p>
      </div>
      <ul class="legend">
        <li><span class="swatch" style="background: var(--s1)"></span>Made playoffs</li>
        <li><span class="swatch" style="background: var(--udfa); opacity: 0.6"></span>Missed playoffs</li>
        <li><span class="swatch" style="background: var(--s1); box-shadow: 0 0 0 2px var(--ink)"></span>Won World Series</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="chart" data-chart="strip"></div>
    </figure>

    <section class="measure notes">
      <h2>Explore a team</h2>
      <p class="team-links">
        {latestTeams
          .slice()
          .sort((a, b) => a.name.localeCompare(b.name))
          .map((t, i, arr) => (
            <>
              <a href={`${base}velocity/teams/${slug(t)}/`}>{t.name}</a>
              {i < arr.length - 1 ? " · " : ""}
            </>
          ))}
      </p>

      <h2>How we did this</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Velocity.</strong> Release speed of every regular-season four-seam fastball, as classified and measured by
        Statcast. We use four-seamers because nearly every pitcher throws one and it is the standard measure of how hard a
        pitcher throws. Statcast’s tracking hardware changed in 2020 (from radar to optical cameras), which may account for
        a small part of any shift around that season.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Pitchers.</strong> Season results come from Baseball Savant. A pitcher is a starter if at least half his
        appearances were starts. Pitchers must have thrown at least {data.meta.minFF} four-seamers and pitched
        {data.meta.minIP.SP} innings as a starter or {data.meta.minIP.RP} in relief; both minimums are scaled down for the
        60-game 2020 season. Correlations compare each pitcher with the average for his role that season, so the
        league-wide rise in velocity and strikeouts doesn’t inflate them.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Teams.</strong> Staff velocity is the average of every four-seamer the team threw. Records, runs allowed
        and playoff results come from the MLB Stats API. Correlations describe association, not cause.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</Base>

<script>
  import data from "../../data/velocity.json";
  import { ridgeline, multiLine, changeBars, seasonDots } from "../../charts/velocity.js";
  import { seasonLine } from "../../charts/compare.js";
  import { scatter, tierDot } from "../../charts/scatter.js";
  import { NICKNAMES, PLAYOFF_SHORT, allTeams, record, signed, slug, yoyBands } from "../../lib/velocity.js";

  const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
  const labels = data.meta.playoffLabels;
  const el = (name) => document.querySelector(`[data-chart="${name}"]`);
  const L = data.seasons.map((s) => s.league);
  const latest = data.seasons[data.seasons.length - 1];
  const teams = allTeams(data);
  const tier = (p) => (p === 5 ? 2 : p > 0 ? 1 : 0);
  const pctFmt = (v) => `${Math.round(v * 100)}%`;

  let metric = "k";
  let pSeason = latest.season;

  const METRICS = {
    k: { label: "Strikeout %", format: (v) => `${v}%`, value: (p) => p.k, reverse: false },
    era: { label: "ERA", format: (v) => v.toFixed(1), value: (p) => p.era, reverse: true, domain: [0, 8] },
    w: { label: "Wins", format: (v) => v.toFixed(0), value: (p) => p.w, reverse: false, startersOnly: true },
  };

  const draw = {
    ridge: () =>
      ridgeline(
        el("ridge"),
        L.map((l) => ({ label: String(l.season), hist: l.hist, avg: l.ff })),
        data.meta.bins,
      ),
    roles: () =>
      multiLine(
        el("roles"),
        [
          { label: "Relievers", color: "var(--s2)", points: L.map((l) => ({ season: l.season, v: l.ffRP })) },
          { label: "Starters", color: "var(--s1)", points: L.map((l) => ({ season: l.season, v: l.ffSP })) },
        ],
        { format: (v) => v.toFixed(1), tipFormat: (v) => `${v.toFixed(1)} mph` },
      ),
    share98: () => seasonLine(el("share98"), L.map((l) => ({ season: l.season, v: l.share98 })), { yLabel: "Of four-seamers at 98+ mph" }),
    pitchers: () => {
      const m = METRICS[metric];
      const season = data.seasons.find((s) => s.season === pSeason);
      const pts = season.pitchers
        .filter((p) => !m.startersOnly || p.role === "SP")
        .filter((p) => m.value(p) != null)
        .map((p) => ({ ...p, x: p.ff, y: Math.min(m.value(p), m.domain ? m.domain[1] : Infinity) }));
      const fastest = [...pts].sort((a, b) => b.x - a.x)[0];
      document.querySelector("[data-role-legend]").hidden = !!m.startersOnly;
      scatter(el("pitchers"), pts, {
        x: { label: "Four-seam velocity (mph)", format: (v) => v.toFixed(0) },
        y: { label: m.label, format: m.format, reverse: m.reverse, domain: m.domain },
        dot: (d) => ({ fill: d.role === "SP" ? "var(--s1)" : "var(--s2)", opacity: 0.7, r: 4 }),
        tip: (d) =>
          `<strong>${d.name}</strong> <span class="muted">${d.role === "SP" ? "Starter" : "Reliever"}, ${d.season}</span><br>${d.ff.toFixed(1)} mph four-seamer<br>${d.k}% strikeouts · ${d.era.toFixed(2)} ERA · ${d.w}-${d.l}<br><span class="muted">${d.ip} innings</span>`,
        label: (d) => (d === fastest ? d.name : null),
      });
    },
    yoyK: () =>
      changeBars(el("yoyK"), yoyBands(data.yoy, "dK"), { format: (v) => signed(v, 1, " pts"), good: "up", title: "Change in strikeout rate" }),
    yoyERA: () =>
      changeBars(el("yoyERA"), yoyBands(data.yoy, "dERA"), { format: (v) => signed(v, 2), good: "down", title: "Change in ERA" }),
    teams: () =>
      scatter(
        el("teams"),
        teams.map((t) => ({ ...t, x: t.rel, y: t.winPct })),
        {
          x: { label: "Staff velocity vs. league average (mph)", format: (v) => signed(v, 1) },
          y: { label: "Regular-season win %", format: pctFmt, domain: [0.2, 0.8] },
          dot: (d) => tierDot(tier(d.playoff)),
          order: (d) => tier(d.playoff),
          tip: (d) =>
            `<strong>${d.season} ${NICKNAMES[d.id]}</strong><br>${record(d)} · ${labels[d.playoff]}<br><span class="muted">${d.ff.toFixed(1)} mph (${signed(d.rel, 1)} vs. league)</span>`,
          label: (d) => (d.season === latest.season && d.playoff === 5 ? `${d.season} ${NICKNAMES[d.id]}` : null),
        },
      ),
    strip: () =>
      seasonDots(
        el("strip"),
        data.seasons.map((s) => ({ season: s.season, teams: s.teams.map((t) => ({ ...t, rel: t.ff - s.league.ff })) })),
        {
          name: (t) => NICKNAMES[t.id],
          tipHtml: (t, row) =>
            `<strong>${row.season} ${NICKNAMES[t.id]}</strong><br>${t.ff.toFixed(1)} mph (${signed(t.rel, 1)} vs. league)<br>${record(t)}${t.playoff ? ` · ${PLAYOFF_SHORT[t.playoff]}` : ""}`,
          href: (t) => `${base}velocity/teams/${slug(t)}/`,
        },
      ),
  };

  const drawAll = () => Object.values(draw).forEach((f) => f());
  drawAll();

  let lastWidth = window.innerWidth;
  window.addEventListener("resize", () => {
    if (window.innerWidth === lastWidth) return;
    lastWidth = window.innerWidth;
    drawAll();
  });

  const wire = (group, attr, onPick) =>
    document.querySelectorAll(`[${group}] button`).forEach((btn) => {
      btn.addEventListener("click", () => {
        document.querySelectorAll(`[${group}] button`).forEach((b) => b.setAttribute("aria-pressed", String(b === btn)));
        onPick(btn.dataset[attr]);
        draw.pitchers();
      });
    });
  wire("data-metric", "metric", (v) => (metric = v));
  wire("data-pseason", "season", (v) => (pSeason = Number(v)));
</script>
